battle_anim.c: the remake layer learns which battle animation runs, when a
move puts up its own background, and when a move draws a battler into a
background.

LaunchBattleAnimation starts every battle animation (a move's, a status
condition's, the general and special ones); the remake layer's hook records
the table and the index (the game keeps them in a static it never reads).
Once the script is set to run, a move's animation may wait at its start
(RemakeHoldAnimation): while the page's remake draws the battle in 3D, the
game's effects begin when its 3D attacker gets there (its breath leaving its
mouth), not before. A contact move's animation instead runs while the 3D
attacker travels and waits at its hit (RunAnimScriptCommand looks ahead
through the commands that run together, up to the next delay or wait, for
the first hit splat or shake of the foe): its splat, shake and sound land
with the 3D blow, and if the blow lands first, what is left of its lead-in
hurries (WaitAnimFrameCount).
LoadMoveBg puts a move's background in the battle background's place (BG3's
map and tiles); the hook records which one, so the remake shows its arena
only while the main background is up. MoveBattlerSpriteToBG draws a
battler's sprite into BG1 or BG2 (monbg: the copy then moves as the
background scrolls, over or instead of the sprite); the hook records which
battler and palette, so the remake draws the battler there too.

